[=#database]
= Database Configuration =

SQL Relay can be configured to connect to a wide variety of databases.

* [oracleconfiguration.html#db-oracle Oracle]
* [mssqlodbcconfiguration.html#db-mssql-odbc Microsoft SQL Server (via ODBC)]
* [mssqlfreetdsconfiguration.html#db-mssql-freetds Microsoft SQL Server (via FreeTDS)]
* [sapconfiguration.html#db-sap SAP/Sybase (via the native SAP/Sybase library)]
* [sapfreetdsconfiguration.html#db-sap-freetds SAP/Sybase (via FreeTDS)]
* [db2configuration.html#db-db2 IBM DB2]
* [informixconfiguration.html#db-informix Informix]
* [mysqlconfiguration.html#db-mysql MySQL/MariaDB]
* [postgresqlconfiguration.html#db-postgresql PostgreSQL]
* [firebirdconfiguration.html#db-firebird Firebird]
* [sqliteconfiguration.html#db-sqlite SQLite]
* [teradataconfiguration.html#db-odbc-teradata Teradata (via ODBC)]
* [exasolconfiguration.html#db-odbc-exasol Exasol (via ODBC)]
* [hiveconfiguration.html#db-odbc-hive Apache Hive (via ODBC)]
* [impalaconfiguration.html#db-odbc-impala Apache Impala (via ODBC)]
* [redshiftodbcconfiguration.html#db-odbc-redshift Amazon Redshift (via ODBC)]
* [redshiftpostgresqlconfiguration.html#db-postgresql-redshift Amazon Redshift (via PostgreSQL)]
* [athenaconfiguration.html#db-odbc-athena Amazon Athena (via ODBC)]
* [odbcconfiguration.html#db-odbc Generic ODBC]

